diff --git a/docs/tee-soft-keybox-update.md b/docs/tee-soft-keybox-update.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f407f94
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/tee-soft-keybox-update.md
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# TEE Soft Emu Keybox online update
+
+## Scope and agreed behavior
+
+- Advanced child page in LineageParts; user-entered HTTP/HTTPS URL starts empty.
+  No bundled source, example URL or URL hint. RAW is the default; Base64 is explicit.
+- Manual updates only. No scheduler, boot receiver, retry loop or RKP changes.
+- Downloads and local imports share a process-wide worker and installation path.
+  Both use installation-time XML/required-field checks only, not cryptographic validation.
+- Existing Keystore2/PureSoft generation, material consumption and ASTER gates stay unchanged.
+  Updating material does not enable TEE Soft Emu or rewrite existing keys/certificates.
+
+## Implementation
+
+- `TeeSoftDebugConfig`: synchronized read/merge/atomic write of config.conf. Each page writes
+  only its own fields; installation owns keybox_path. Unknown key/value fields survive edits.
+- `KeyboxUpdater`: one active import/update across page recreation, bounded HTTP download,
+  explicit Base64 decoding, shared validation and keybox.xml installation.
+- `KeyboxXmlValidator`: UTF-8, one complete XML document, at least one Key with nonempty
+  PrivateKey and Certificate. Also accepts an ungrouped legacy document with both fields.
+  Optional count, device ID and algorithm metadata are not required. Mixed or incomplete
+  sibling groups cannot contribute fields to one another. XML comments are accepted;
+  DTDs, nested Key entries and nested payload elements are rejected. CDATA/entity payloads
+  are rejected because the existing consumer extracts literal tag contents.
+- Per response/XML limit: 1 MiB; XML depth: 64; token count: 100000. Base64 permits spaces,
+  tabs and CR/LF; invalid alphabet content fails. HTTP requires status 200, at most five
+  redirects, 15-second connection/read timeouts and a 60-second elapsed-time budget checked
+  between blocking calls. An in-progress blocking call may exceed that budget by its timeout.
+  HTTPS redirects cannot downgrade to HTTP. Userinfo and URL fragments are not accepted.
+- Installation writes, sets existing 0644 permissions, syncs and renames a same-directory
+  temporary file. A backup copy restores the previous file if subsequent config activation
+  fails. Normal completion removes temporary files. Config and material are separate files:
+  this is not a crash-atomic transaction across both, and abrupt process/device termination
+  can leave a temporary/backup file. Failed rollback preserves its backup for recovery.
+- Result codes persist separately from the last successful update timestamp. No user URL,
+  response or private key is logged. Success means material was installed, not that its
+  signatures are valid or that attestation will be accepted.
+- Manifest adds INTERNET and permits HTTP for user-defined sources. Existing system_app
+  networking and adbroot file create/rename policies cover these operations; no new policy
+  or Keystore2 IPC is introduced.
+
+## Static verification (2026-11-13)
+
+- Java tree-sitter syntax parsing: passed for all five teedebug Java files.
+- Manifest, preference XML and all three new locale resource files: XML parsing passed.
+- Resource references, fragment navigation/retention, API availability, existing file/network
+  SELinux permissions and failure/concurrency paths: checked statically.
+- Whitespace check: git diff --check passed.
+- No compilation, executable behavior tests, network fetch or device verification performed.
+
+## Remaining runtime validation
+
+After a future build: RAW/Base64 success, download/decode/XML rejection preserving old
+material, write/config activation failures and rollback, config field preservation across
+both pages, local/network exclusion, recreation/back navigation during a job, SELinux
+access and subsequent Keystore2 consumption. Structural validation deliberately cannot
+reject all unusable cryptographic material.
